## Linux amd64 real protocol

Go 1.27.3 and PostgreSQL 18.6. Evidence:
  /root/lane-sch-tools/selectedqueue.dDEO57fm

An isolated network-none PG container, a private socket relay and a route-free
network namespace ran -race -tags repository_integration and passed these seven:

- TestPostgresPreflightUsesOneSnapshotAndRefreshes
- TestPostgresPreflightRequiresReadOnlyScopedSnapshot
- TestPostgresQueueExecutorUsesSelectedOwnerSnapshot
- TestPostgresQueueExecutorRejectsWrongModeAndScope
- TestPostgresWorkspaceQueueUsesLiveCommittedShares
- TestPostgresWorkspaceQueueRejectsForeignAndMissingScope
- TestPostgresWorkspaceQueueRefusesForeignReservationCoordinates

The same invocation passed TestQueueExecutorSnapshotRejectsUnborrowedInputs
and all four subcases. The selected test persisted queue rows, committed a
different job's hold and a new enqueue concurrently, retained the original
snapshot order, refreshed both in a new snapshot and preserved owner rows,
revisions and the exact sole competing hold. The legacy tests retained their
constant aggregate-query and foreign-scope refusal assertions.

source-head matches the tested SHA, source.diff is empty and the manifest
verifies. The PG DSN/password and owned container were removed; no port was
exposed and no own service remains. Earlier exit-75 attempts were resource
preflights before any fixture/test, not failed PG results.
The native runner keeps 3072 MiB free/12288 MiB available, 15 GiB disk,
full I/O avg10/avg60 at most 5%, serial global/lane locks and a bounded
30-second foreground lock wait. It has no background retry queue.

